# SecureSuite — Full Database Integration & Feature Build-out

Replace all mock/hardcoded data with live queries from the `vidhi_insurance` MySQL database, and build out every placeholder module into a fully working feature.

## Database Schema Summary

Your `vidhi_insurance` database has **18 tables**. The key business tables are:

| Table | Purpose | Rows relate to |
|---|---|---|
| `agents` | Agent master (name, email, phone, brokerage rate) | customers, policies |
| `customers` | Customer master (name, email, phone, address, agent_id) | agents, policies, claims, healths |
| `policies` | Core policy records (numbers, dates, premiums, insurer, type) | customers, agents, motors, fires, healths, payments, claims |
| `claims_master` | Claims (claim_no, loss details, status, settlement) | customers, policies |
| `payments` | Premium payments (type, cheque/bank, amount, date) | policies |
| `motors` | Motor-specific policy data (vehicle reg, engine, chassis) | policies |
| `fires` | Fire-specific policy data (risk location, valuations) | policies |
| `healths` | Health-specific member data (member name, DOB, relation) | policies, customers |
| `agent_brokerages` | Agent commission payouts | agents |
| `company_brokerages` | Brokerage received from insurers | — |
| `quotations` | Quote proposals linked to policies | policies |
| `timeline_entries` | Activity log per policy | policies |
| `users` | Login users (name, email, username, password, role) | — |

